<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis II of Hungary</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1506–1526</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Louis II of Bohemia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> was the Jagiellonian king of Hungary and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> from 1516. Faced with a weak treasury and quarrelling nobles, he could not resist the Ottoman advance. He was killed fleeing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mohacs">Battle of Mohács</a> in 1526, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a> destroyed the Hungarian army, and his death led to the division of Hungary between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-zapolya">John Zápolya</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-ii-of-hungary.jpg" alt="Louis II of Hungary" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Krell · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hans_Krell_-_Portrait_of_King_Louis_II_of_Hungary_(c.1526).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
